  "scope": "The product adapter now owns RetentionPolicy, CompactionReport, defaults, batch ceiling, semantic policy admission and pure removal-count arithmetic. Released VM paths are exact reexports; LSV2301 and serde field/unknown-field behavior remain unchanged. Memory and SQLite journals share numeric batch sizing but retain eligible logical-unit selection, live-group protection, ordering, audit cascade and storage ownership. Memory compaction first measures every selected payload using the existing bounded JSON codec; it commits map removals only after all checks pass, avoiding temporary JSON output buffers. Five private corrupt-state fixtures exercise oversized merge plans/results, local completions, dispatch requests and retry metadata, preserving exact LSV3002 labels, all maps, audits and local inputs on refusal. The pre-fix test demonstrates partial deletion; successful behavior matches the frozen previous implementation across 20 retention/batch combinations. SQLite keeps its immediate transaction and unchanged deletion/replay reconciliation. This is in-process failure protection, not proof that malformed values can enter through public admission, allocation-failure recovery, crash durability or full native repository extraction.",
